  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Sunshine-31c50c9aa85f4ff6.mp3",
    "speaker": "Sunshine",
    "text": "[warmly] Okay, let me get a look at them. These four are... well, they're sentence-ending particles. They don't have a meaning of their own, they add a mood. All four are neutral tone, so they're light and quick, and they tuck in right at the end of a sentence. And look, they all start with the same piece.",
    "duration": 18.364082,
    "running_start_time": 54.758369000000016,
    "alignment": "Sunshine-31c50c9aa85f4ff6.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
    "source_id": null,
    "duration": 0.2,
    "running_start_time": 73.12245100000001
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Rob-cbb300c00b27960b.mp3",
    "speaker": "Rob",
    "text": "[curious] The little square box on the left? It looks like an open mouth.",
    "duration": 3.970612,
    "running_start_time": 73.32245100000002,
    "alignment": "Rob-cbb300c00b27960b.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
    "source_id": null,
    "duration": 0.2,
    "running_start_time": 77.29306300000002
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Sunshine-90c02854cbfd77f8.mp3",
    "speaker": "Sunshine",
    "text": "Exactly. That's the mouth radical. It makes sense, since these are all sounds you make with your mouth. The right side is a hint at the sound.",
    "duration": 8.907755,
    "running_start_time": 77.49306300000002,
    "alignment": "Sunshine-90c02854cbfd77f8.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
    "source_id": null,
    "duration": 0.2,
    "running_start_time": 86.40081800000002
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "line",
    "source_id": "Rob-6eddfe6e224b2766.mp3",
    "speaker": "Rob",
    "text": "Because humans make sounds with mouths, right?",
    "duration": 3.160816,
    "running_start_time": 86.60081800000002,
    "alignment": "Rob-6eddfe6e224b2766.json"
  },
  {
    "segment_type": "gap",
